  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_112' aria-label=\" Manjit Singh & Anr. versus Darshana Devi & Ors.  pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('112','2024','2024_11_876_885','2024INSC895'); ><font size='4'> <strong>MANJIT SINGH & ANR.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>DARSHANA DEVI & ORS.  </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 11 S.C.R. 876</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 895</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010006812024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.B. PARDIWALA, R MAHADEVAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration High Court held that the appellants-subsequent purchasers could not be said to be bona fide purchasers in accordance with Section 19 (b) of the Specific Relief Act, 1963 and decreed the suit of the plaintiff granting specific performance of oral agreement of sale between defendant (owner of the suit property). Headnotes&dagger; Specific Relief Act, 1963 &ndash; s.19(b) &ndash; General Clauses Act &ndash; s.3(22) &ndash; Bhartiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 &ndash; s.2(11) &ndash; &ldquo;good faith&rdquo; &ndash; Oral agreement for sale of the suit property between<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 21-11-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 13066/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('112','2024','2024_11_876_885','2024INSC895','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('112','2024','2024_11_876_885',